    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Weapon (Maul), Artifact (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>The elementium Maul <em>Sulfuras</em> is the weapon of Ragnaros, the Elemental Lord of Fire. In the beginning, the four elemental lords warred against one another for dominance over the nascent Azeroth. While the other elemental lords fought with mastery of their own elements, Ragnaros used <em>Sulfuras</em> to turn their elements against them, boiling seas, choking the skies with smoke and embers, and turning mountains into erupting volcanoes.</p><p><strong>Magic Weapon.</strong> You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. A creature hit by this weapon takes an extra 1d10 Fire damage and starts &amp;Reference[Burning apply=false], taking 1d10 Fire damage at the start of each of its turns instead of the normal burning damage.</p><p><strong>Ignite the Elements.</strong> While holding this weapon, you can take a Magic action to produce one of the following effects. Once an effect has been used, that effect can’t be used again until the next dawn:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Boiling Point.</strong> You cause any container or body of water within 1 mile of you to boil for 1 minute. A creature that enters the boiling water or starts its turn there takes 2d10 Fire damage.</p></li><li><p><strong>Embersmoke.</strong> You cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplIncendiary]{Incendiary Cloud} (save DC 18) from the weapon.</p></li><li><p><strong>Eruption.</strong> You make lava erupt in a 10-foot-radius, 60-foot-high Cylinder centered on a point on the ground you can see within 120 feet. Each creature in that area makes a DC 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 9d10 Fire damage plus 9d10 Bludgeoning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> <em>Sulfuras</em> has the following random properties:</p><ul><li><p>1 minor beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 major beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 minor detrimental property</p></li><li><p>1 major detrimental property</p></li></ul><p><strong>Destroying Sulfuras.</strong> In an underwater tunnel network deep beneath Vashj’ir lies an abandoned, heavily trapped temple to Neptulon, the Elemental Lord of Water. Placing <em>Sulfuras</em> on the temple’s central altar quenches its fire permanently, rendering it nonmagical and destructible.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-MdS5HJsGC88BVXiC\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Après un coup, appliquez l’effet de <em>Set Ablaze</em> ; <em>Burning Damage</em> inflige les 1d10 Fire au début de chaque tour de la cible. Pour <em>Boiling Point</em>, <em>Boiling Water</em> inflige les 2d10 Fire. Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ.</p></section>",
